'''
Approach:
1. Consider the parity of each element in nums1.
2. If all elements in nums1 are even, choosing nums2[i] = nums1[i] for all i makes 
   nums2 all even.
3. If there is at least one odd element in nums1:
   - For indices where nums1[i] is odd, choose nums2[i] = nums1[i] (odd).
   - For indices where nums1[i] is even, choose nums2[i] = nums1[i] - nums1[j] 
     where j is any index with an odd value. Since even - odd = odd, nums2[i] is odd.
   Thus, nums2 can be made all odd.
4. In all possible cases, a valid construction exists. Therefore, the answer is 
   always true.

Time Complexity: O(1).
Space Complexity: O(1).
